  "assessment": {
    "traffic": "The native kernel records only 50.47% of the inclusive bridge L2 system-memory sector-byte proxy yet is 56.82% slower, so compressed-weight traffic reduction is already visible and external-memory volume is not the closing bottleneck in this profile.",
    "tensor_feed": "Native Tensor throughput is 37.51% versus 92.48% for the cuBLASLt BF16 body despite 1.94x achieved occupancy.",
    "decode_and_shared": "Native executes 4.24x the total instructions, executes exactly 800x as many ordinary shared-load SASS instructions as the BF16 kernel, has no LDSM fragment feed, and records 25.89 million raw shared bank conflicts where the bridge records none. PairLookup explains 24.72 million excessive shared wavefronts; the B/scale LDGSTS destination layout explains another 16.36 million.",
    "global_access": "The native A cp.async.ca and B/scale cp.async.cg paths are proven active by both SASS and exact dynamic LDGSTS counts. The B/scale request-to-sector estimate is about 63.43%, but LDGSTS metric domains must not be mixed when deriving totals.",
    "epilogue": "Native L1 global-write sector bytes are exactly 2x the logical BF16 output size. Source ownership maps each warp to eight separated 16-byte row spans, which forces eight 32-byte sectors for 128 useful bytes.",
    "next_complete_cell": [
      "replace conflict-heavy scalar PairLookup feeding with a conflict-free decoder and fragment feed",
      "redesign the 48-byte packed-B/scale shared layout and LDGSTS destination mapping",
      "coalesce the packed BF16 epilogue",
      "evaluate a three-slot load/decode/MMA pipeline only as part of the complete resource-qualified cell",
      "preserve exact accumulation order, no spills, and at least 16 resident warps per SM",
      "qualify Gate/Up and Down as separate exact-shape specializations"
    ],
